GDV1-3169 | Description in file tickets/GDV1-3169.md | 2025-12-16 | Delete Command for remote module wipe | Implemented DeleteModule command: added DELETE_MODULE enum, checkIsModuleDeleted() REST API endpoint, handleDeleteModule() with server verification and factory reset via ClearModuleDataService. Moved IClearModuleDataService to Core/Domain/Interfaces. Processes via existing ModuleCommandNotification flow. | Impact: critical functionality for secure module deletion from system.
GDV1-3182 | Description in file tickets/GDV1-3182.md | 2025-12-18 | Automatic Module Reset After Prolonged Offline State | Implemented checkOfflineStateAndTriggerReboot() in DiagnosticService: tracks continuous offline duration (WiFi down OR MQTT+API down), applies module-type-specific thresholds (15 min for MODULE_TYPE_SENSOR, 4h for other modules), sets noScanSensors flag and BOOT_TYPE_TECHNICAL, triggers restart via CONFIGURED_NEED_RESTART for graceful recovery. | Impact: automatic recovery from prolonged connectivity failures, eliminates manual intervention for stuck modules, improves system reliability.
GDV1-3211 | Description in file tickets/GDV1-3211.md | 2026-01-08 | Check Module Deletion Status on Every Startup | Implemented checkModuleDeletionOnStartup() in ModuleSetupService: queries server via hybridApiService->checkIsModuleDeleted() after WiFi connection during startup in ConfigureDoneModeConfigure(). If module marked as deleted on server, automatically sets mode to USER_CAN_CONFIGURE (42), clears all data via ClearModuleDataService, and triggers restart. Added IHybridAPIService, IClearModuleDataService, IArduinoAdapter dependencies to ModuleSetupService. Graceful error handling for network failures. | Impact: ensures consistency between server and hardware states, automatically handles offline deletion scenarios, prevents deleted modules from operating after restart, critical for system integrity.
GDV1-3224 | Description in file tickets/GDV1-3224.md | 2026-01-17 | Per-Feature Configurable Logging Channels (MQTT/Serial/Both) | Extended debug feature system to support per-feature logging channel configuration. Added getLogChannel()/setLogChannel() methods to IDebugFeature, updated IDebugSystem::registerFeature() with channel parameter, implemented setFeatureLogChannel() for runtime updates. Added NEW overloaded logger methods (print/println/printf) with MqttLoggerMode channelOverride parameter in ILogger/MqttLogger. Added helper methods shouldLogToMqtt(mode)/shouldLogToSerial(mode). All features default to SerialOnly, can be changed at runtime. 100% backward compatible - NO existing method signatures or implementations modified. | Impact: Low risk, high flexibility - All existing code works unchanged, new functionality available through new overloaded methods only. Enables granular control of debug output routing (MQTT/Serial/Both) per feature at runtime. Clean architecture maintained - logger remains independent of debug system.
